target:    .github/workflows/main.yml
gate:      composer test:perf-gate-integrity
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    which is not pinned to a commit
rationale: Puts the wordpress.org deploy action back on @stable. main.yml fires on `push: tags: - "*"` and holds SVN_USERNAME and SVN_PASSWORD for a plugin with ~70,000 active installs -- so whatever the `stable` BRANCH points at on the day someone cuts a tag is what receives those credentials and publishes to the wordpress.org repository. `stable` is a branch, not even a tag; every push to it lands straight in that step. The gate checks EVERY `uses:` line, and it evaluates against the comment-stripped copy that section 5 already builds -- the obvious spelling of this check, 'a 40-hex SHA appears', is satisfied by the SHA sitting in the explanatory comment beside each pin.
---
--- a/.github/workflows/main.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/main.yml
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@
       # the same commit as tag 2.3.0 — so this froze the action without changing what runs.
       # `stable` is a branch: every push to it would otherwise have shipped straight into the
       # step that publishes to the WordPress.org SVN repository.
-      uses: 10up/action-wordpress-plugin-deploy@54bd289b8525fd23a5c365ec369185f2966529c2 # 2.3.0
+      uses: 10up/action-wordpress-plugin-deploy@stable
       env:
         SVN_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.SVN_PASSWORD }}
         SVN_USERNAME: ${{ secrets.SVN_USERNAME }}
